package mcp

import "github.com/KoJaco/ambit/internal/core"

// Authoring tool descriptions include modeling guidance; keep aligned with
// docs/contracts/arch-model-format.md (Modeling guidance) and mcp-tools.md.
var (
	seedModelDescription = `Propose a model from a harness-generated graph (staged, not applied; canonical model unchanged until architect accepts).

Optional node id: a free lowercase slug you choose, so parent_id and relationships can reference nodes created in this same call. Nodes in one call may reference each other in parent_id and depends_on in any order. Relationship kind is one of sync, async or data. Shared code (types, helpers, conventions several nodes use) belongs in one node that owns it, with the other nodes listing it in depends_on, so it is built once and every agent sees it in their brief. protected: true on a node makes its implementation paths off-limits to every other node (check_scope and ambit check flag edits, and briefs list them as off-limits); use it for generated or hand-curated files. Optional risk (low|medium|high), review (none|required) and verify (commands that prove the node works) feed the brief, check_done and the completion policy. Files no node should own (generated output, lockfiles, vendored code) are not modelled: they are excluded from drift with drift_ignore globs in .arch/config.json. Optional updates, delete_relationships and delete_nodes restructure an existing model in one proposal (accept is all-or-nothing). A relationship with the same from, to and label as an existing edge updates it in place; pass relationship_id to change an existing edge's label, kind or endpoints. An update may carry new_id to rename a node. ` + proposalMetaGuidance + `

Modeling: use parent_id for containment/drill-down; use relationships for runtime flow (calls, delegates, hosts, stages) between nodes at a level — not for every sibling pair. Every node should be reachable from the product root via parent_id. External actors (harness, browser): type external, one directed inbound edge per channel. Thin entry nodes should relate to the module they host (e.g. entry hosts tool surface). See docs/contracts/arch-model-format.md Modeling guidance. ` + core.ShallowModelGuidance + " " + core.AuthoringGuidance + " " + contractGuidance + " " + buildPlanFieldsGuidance

	setRelationshipDescription = `Propose creating or updating a cross-cutting relationship (staged, not applied). Directed edge: from, to, label, kind (sync|async|data). Do not use for parent/child — use parent_id on create_node/update_node. Add edges for control/data flow you need on the canvas; omit when hierarchy alone is enough. Optional contract {format: openapi|jsonschema|text, ref: repo path, text}: what is on the wire, so both ends build to one interface; omitted leaves an existing contract unchanged, {} clears it. Endpoints must name existing node ids. An edge with the same from, to and label is updated in place (no duplicate); pass relationship_id to change an existing edge's endpoints, label or kind. ` + proposalMetaGuidance + ` See docs/contracts/arch-model-format.md Modeling guidance. ` + core.ShallowModelGuidance

	deleteRelationshipDescription = "Propose deleting one relationship (edge) by relationship_id (staged, not applied). Deleting an edge also removes any nodes inside it (relationship interior). Nodes at the endpoints are kept."

	listIconsDescription = "List the allowed icon ids with a one-line label each. Use these ids for the icon field of create_node, update_node and seed_model nodes."

	buildPlanFieldsGuidance = "Optional build-planning fields on nodes: external (true: outside the build, such as a third-party service; left out of the build order), human_gates ([{kind: decision|credential|phone|deploy_approval|install, note}]: steps only a person can do; the person clears them in the UI), deliverables (repo-relative paths the node must produce, checked by check_deliverables and check_done), references (repo-relative docs the spec or contract must stay in sync with, checked by check_contract_sync), shared (true: this node owns shared manifests such as go.mod, package.json and lockfiles), milestones ([{id, label, status pending|in_progress|done}]: a node finished in stages stops at needs_review until all are done) and gates (ids of nodes that wait for this node, for a spike: each listed node effectively depends on it; must exist and stay acyclic)."

	createNodeDescription = `Propose one new node (staged, not applied). Optional id: a lowercase slug you choose (letters, digits, single hyphens) so later calls can reference this node in parent_id or edges; rejected if taken or reserved by another pending proposal. Set parent_id for hierarchy (or relationship_id for relationship interior). Put runtime wiring in set_relationship, not parent_id. See docs/contracts/arch-model-format.md Modeling guidance. ` + core.ShallowModelGuidance + " " + core.AuthoringGuidance + " " + contractGuidance + " " + buildPlanFieldsGuidance

	updateNodeDescription = "Propose changes to a node (staged, not applied). " + core.ShallowModelGuidance + " " + contractGuidance + " Omitted depends_on/contract are unchanged; depends_on [] and contract {} clear them (so do [] for human_gates, deliverables, references, milestones and gates). " + buildPlanFieldsGuidance + " new_id renames the node (see rename_node); status is not settable here (use update_node_status) and edges are changed with set_relationship. Moving a node (parent_id) and setting depends_on in one proposal is checked against the final tree. " + proposalMetaGuidance

	contractGuidance = "Put interfaces in the structured contract field (payloads, invariants, errors, owns_data), not in the spec prose. Set depends_on only for real build ordering (this node needs those nodes built first), not for flow direction; relationships already express flow. A dependency cycle is rejected. Call get_build_order before building."

	setConstraintsDescription = "Propose replacing the project-wide rules (staged, not applied; replace-all, so send the full list). Each constraint: id (slug), text (1..300 chars), severity must (default) or should. Max 24. Every agent brief shows these rules, so keep them short and checkable."

	renameNodeDescription = "Propose changing a node id (staged, not applied). Accepting rewrites the id in the node file names, parent_id and depends_on of other nodes, relationships, the active assignment, cached layouts and the spec file name; implementation globs and prose are left unchanged. Rejected when new_id is taken, reserved by another pending proposal, or not a lowercase slug. Inside one proposal refer to the node by its current id; renames apply last. update_node also accepts new_id."

	withdrawProposalDescription = "Withdraw a pending proposal you staged in this session (it stays queryable as withdrawn). Only the session that staged a proposal can withdraw it; the architect can always delete it in the UI. To replace a pending proposal in one step, pass supersedes: <proposal_id> when staging the new one."

	proposalMetaGuidance = "Optional on every staging tool: change_set (slug that groups related proposals in the UI), supersedes (id of a pending proposal you staged in this session; it is withdrawn once the new one is staged, and its create ids are free to reuse) and depends_on_proposal (id of a pending proposal; this one is validated against the model as it will be once that one is accepted, and cannot be accepted while it is pending)."

	getBuildOrderDescription = "Return the advisory build order (read-only, from depends_on and gates): order with wave, class, depends_on, blocked_by, gates, gated_by, human_gates (with cleared state) and done per buildable node, plus waves (parallelisable layers), cycles and unordered. class is agent-parallel (an agent can build it once unblocked), needs-human (it has human gates not yet cleared by the person at the UI) or blocked (an unfinished dependency or status blocked). Nodes flagged external are left out of order and waves and listed in externals; they never block. ready_now lists the ordered nodes that are not blocked, not done and not external; max_parallel and parallel_set are a greedy packing of the agent-parallel nodes in ready_now into nodes whose implementation globs do not overlap, so they can be built at once. Optional scope_node_id limits it to a subtree, compact returns only id, class and wave per node (about a tenth of the size, plus ready_now and parallel_set), ready_only returns only the nodes in ready_now. Call this before building to pick nodes to start."

	checkDeliverablesDescription = "Check that each deliverable path the node declares exists and is non-empty (a file with content, or a directory holding a non-empty file). Read-only. Pass worktree to look in a git worktree. A path that escapes the repository is reported unsafe and never read. Documentation deliverables are written by the parent agent, not by a subagent; run this to confirm they are in place."

	runVerifyDescription = "Run the node's verify commands, which come only from the model on disk (never from a pending proposal), with sh -c in the checkout (pass worktree for a git worktree). Each command has its own timeout (timeout_s, default 120, max 600) and a minimal environment: a fixed allowlist of variables plus the variables the command names itself. Output is truncated to its last 8 KiB. A command whose binary is missing or that references an unset environment variable is reported not_runnable and is not started. It changes nothing in the model, but the commands are shell commands from the model, so only accept verify commands you would run yourself."

	checkDependentsDescription = "Run run_verify for the direct dependents of a node (nodes whose depends_on names it, or that it gates), to see whether finishing this node broke them. At most 16 dependents per call and 15 minutes in total (dependents not run in time are listed as skipped); dependents without verify commands are listed as skipped. Same environment, timeout and trust rules as run_verify."

	checkContractSyncDescription = "Compare a node with the docs it points at: every path in its references list and the ref of every relationship contract touching it must exist and be non-empty, and the contract must not have changed since the node was last marked in_progress or done (contract_changed). Read-only. Pass worktree for a git worktree."

	subagentGuidance = core.SubagentGuidance
)
